        "thread_id": "TH1",
        "thread_goal": "Align on pilot scope, target audience, and success criteria.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi team, welcome to the official channel for the Frontline Wellbeing & Communication Skills Program. The goal is to design and pilot a program to support our contact centre and reception staff. First step is to align on the pilot scope. I've started a doc for our needs analysis in A1. Per T2, we need to define the target audience. What are your thoughts on which teams should be included?",
            "mentions": [
              45680,
              4784,
              605,
              89425
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for kicking this off. To ensure we get meaningful data without disrupting service levels, I suggest we pilot with two distinct teams: the 'Inbound Complaints' team (12 staff) and the 'General Enquiries' reception desk (4 staff). They face different types of stressors, which would give us good comparative feedback. That's a total of 16 participants.",
            "mentions": [
              56723
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 4784,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "That sounds like a lot of people to take off the phones. Are we sure we can cover the shifts?",
            "mentions": [
              45680
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 605,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Ok, so I need to make a list of the people for T2. Where can I find the official team rosters?",
            "mentions": [
              56723
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "T2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Good point. We won't train them all at once. We can split each team into two groups for staggered sessions. That way we always maintain at least 50% staffing. I can draft a schedule to show how it would work.",
            "mentions": [
              4784
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "I can send you the links to the HR system rosters. Let's first confirm the teams. The proposal from @45680 sounds solid. Any objections to proceeding with the 'Inbound Complaints' and 'General Enquiries' teams for a total of 16 participants?",
            "mentions": [
              605,
              45680
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 4784,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Ok with me if the schedule works.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 605,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "No objections.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": "M6",
            "text": "Great, that's settled then. Decision D1 is confirmed. Now, for success metrics. How will we know if the pilot is successful? I propose we track: 1. A reduction in short-term sick leave days for the pilot group, and 2. Participant feedback via a post-program survey.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D1"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M10",
            "speaker_id": 89425,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "Those are good lagging indicators. For wellbeing, we could also add a simple pre- and post- a 'stress level' score (1-5 scale) in the survey. It's subjective but gives a quick pulse check.",
            "mentions": [
              56723
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M11",
            "speaker_id": 45680,
            "reply_to": "M9",
            "text": "I agree with @89425. And for the communication part, a more direct metric would be better than just survey feedback. Can we track the percentage of calls escalated to a supervisor? A 5% reduction there would be a clear win. We could also look at customer satisfaction scores for the agents involved.",
            "mentions": [
              89425
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "chart_with_upwards_trend",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M12",
            "speaker_id": 56723,
            "reply_to": "M11",
            "text": "Excellent suggestions. So, let's lock in these three primary metrics: 1. Reduction in call escalations, 2. Improvement in self-reported stress levels, and 3. Qualitative feedback from the final survey. Is everyone aligned on this?",
            "mentions": [
              45680,
              89425
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D2"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M13",
